    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30108" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mūsēus</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mūsaeus</span></b> , a, um,
		adj., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μουσεῖος</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to the muses, poetical</i> or <i>musical</i> (<b>poet.</b>): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">musaea mele,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Lucr.
					2, 412</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">musaeo lepōre,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 1,
					934</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vates,</span>”
				i. e. <i>Orpheus</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 2, p. 124</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> For
			musivus, <i>mosaic</i>, Inscr. Spon. Miscell. Sect.
		2.</div>
